    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 8,
      "prompt": "Find the angle $\\theta$ between $\\vec{u}=\\langle 0,2\\rangle$ and $\\vec{v}=\\langle 2,2\\rangle$.",
      "hint": "Use $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}}{\\|\\vec{u}\\|\\,\\|\\vec{v}\\|}$. Each magnitude needs a square root.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Dot product: $\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}=(0)(2)+(2)(2)=4$.",
          "Magnitudes: $\\|\\vec{u}\\|=\\sqrt{0^2+2^2}=2$ and $\\|\\vec{v}\\|=\\sqrt{2^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "So $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{4}{(2)(2\\sqrt{2})}=\\dfrac{4}{4\\sqrt{2}}=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.",
          "The angle with cosine $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ is $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$"
      }
