    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 9,
      "prompt": "Find the scalar projection (component) of $\\vec{u}=\\langle 5,2\\rangle$ onto $\\vec{v}=\\langle 3,4\\rangle$, that is $\\operatorname{comp}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}$.",
      "hint": "The scalar projection is a number: $\\operatorname{comp}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}=\\dfrac{\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}}{\\|\\vec{v}\\|}$. Divide by the magnitude, not its square.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Numerator: $\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}=(5)(3)+(2)(4)=15+8=23$.",
          "Magnitude of $\\vec{v}$: $\\|\\vec{v}\\|=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=\\sqrt{25}=5$.",
          "Scalar projection: $\\operatorname{comp}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}=\\dfrac{23}{5}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\operatorname{comp}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}=\\dfrac{23}{5}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 10,
      "prompt": "Write $\\vec{u}=\\langle 5,2\\rangle$ as the sum of a vector parallel to $\\vec{v}=\\langle 1,1\\rangle$ and a vector orthogonal to $\\vec{v}$.",
      "hint": "The parallel part is $\\operatorname{proj}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}=\\dfrac{\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}}{\\vec{v}\\cdot\\vec{v}}\\,\\vec{v}$. The orthogonal part is $\\vec{u}-\\operatorname{proj}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Parallel part: $\\vec{u}\\cdot\\vec{v}=(5)(1)+(2)(1)=7$ and $\\vec{v}\\cdot\\vec{v}=1^2+1^2=2$.",
          "So $\\vec{w}_1=\\operatorname{proj}_{\\vec{v}}\\vec{u}=\\dfrac{7}{2}\\langle 1,1\\rangle=\\left\\langle \\dfrac{7}{2},\\dfrac{7}{2}\\right\\rangle$.",
          "Orthogonal part: $\\vec{w}_2=\\vec{u}-\\vec{w}_1=\\left\\langle 5-\\dfrac{7}{2},\\,2-\\dfrac{7}{2}\\right\\rangle=\\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2},-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right\\rangle$.",
          "Check orthogonality: $\\vec{w}_2\\cdot\\vec{v}=\\dfrac{3}{2}-\\dfrac{3}{2}=0$, and $\\vec{w}_1+\\vec{w}_2=\\langle 5,2\\rangle=\\vec{u}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\vec{u}=\\left\\langle \\dfrac{7}{2},\\dfrac{7}{2}\\right\\rangle+\\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2},-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right\\rangle$"
      }
    }
  ]
